Phase 11 – Data Refresh Simplification & Cache Removal

Generate Report / Fetch Stories / Load Components / Deployment Readiness Enhancements

⸻

Objective

This phase simplifies the entire report generation workflow by removing unnecessary cache options and ensuring that every operation always retrieves the latest source data from external systems.

The application should no longer depend on previously cached Stories or Components during manual execution.

Instead:

* Fetch Stories → Always from iTrack
* Load Components → Always from GitHub/Kubernetes
* Generate Report → Always use freshly loaded data
* Deployment Refresh → Always refresh Deployment Readiness records

This ensures that release analysis is always based on the latest information.

⸻

Feature 1 – Remove Story Cache Option

Existing Behavior

The Fetch Stories section currently provides:

* Fetch Stories
* Use Cache Data From Database
* Force Fetch From iTrack

This introduces unnecessary complexity and stale data.

⸻

New Requirement

Remove the cache option completely.

Only one action should remain:

Fetch Stories

Every execution must retrieve stories directly from iTrack.

⸻

Acceptance Criteria

* Remove “Use Cache Data From Database” option from UI.
* Remove cache selection dropdown.
* Remove all backend cache-related logic.
* Remove cache-specific controller/service methods.
* Remove cache validation logic.
* Always fetch directly from iTrack.
* Existing functionality must continue without regression.

⸻

Feature 2 – Refresh iTrack Stories Before Saving

Requirement

Whenever Fetch Stories is invoked:

Before fetching data from iTrack,

Delete all existing records for:

* Team Key
* Fix Version

from the iTrack Stories table.

Then insert the latest records.

Never merge with old records.

⸻

Reason

Stories may change during the release window.

Keeping old records can result in:

* stale stories
* removed stories remaining
* modified stories not updated

Every execution should represent the latest iTrack state.

⸻

Acceptance Criteria

Controller Flow

1. Receive Fetch Stories request.
2. Delete existing records using:
    * Team Key
    * Fix Version
3. Fetch latest stories from iTrack.
4. Save latest records.
5. Return latest response.

⸻

Database Changes

Replace every Project Key reference with Team Key.

Primary logical key:

* Team Key
* Fix Version
* Story Number

⸻

Performance Requirement

Do not delete records individually.

Use repository bulk delete operations.

Example:

Delete By TeamKey And FixVersion

Avoid unnecessary database calls.

⸻

